WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.153 --> 00:00:02.543
- We Brusselin'. Everyday we Brusselin'.

00:00:02.543 --> 00:00:04.926
Everyday we do Brusselin'.

00:00:04.926 --> 00:00:07.509
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.988 --> 00:00:16.292
- I hate Brussels sprouts.

00:00:16.292 --> 00:00:18.356
- I hate Brussels sprouts.

00:00:18.356 --> 00:00:21.521
- I think Brussels sprouts
are disgusting and terrible.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:24.238
- I went out to dinner with
my friends from high school

00:00:24.238 --> 00:00:26.325
a few months ago and they forced me

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:28.701
to try Brussels sprouts again.

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:31.769
It was covered in like garlic and bacon

00:00:31.769 --> 00:00:33.128
and it was still disgusting.

00:00:33.128 --> 00:00:35.794
- Being a vegetarian, I
think people often assume

00:00:35.794 --> 00:00:39.465
that I'm typically always
down for Brussels sprouts.

00:00:39.465 --> 00:00:41.894
Like any time I tell
people it's always this

00:00:41.894 --> 00:00:43.467
like shocked reaction.

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:45.091
- I haven't really given it a fair shot,

00:00:45.091 --> 00:00:46.161
but I don't know if I'm gonna give it

00:00:46.161 --> 00:00:48.068
a fair shot today either.

00:00:48.068 --> 00:00:50.424
(electronic music)

00:00:50.424 --> 00:00:51.439
- My name is Ross Pineda,

00:00:51.439 --> 00:00:53.961
currently the junior
sous chef at Pig and Cow.

00:00:53.961 --> 00:00:57.863
- I am @HappyHealthyLatina, AKA Chef Yadi

00:00:57.863 --> 00:01:00.552
and I'm the plant-based people chef.

00:01:00.552 --> 00:01:03.841
I heard we have some picky
eaters with vegetables.

00:01:03.841 --> 00:01:06.362
Brussels sprouts. Dun dun dun!

00:01:06.362 --> 00:01:08.667
I think they have a
little bit of a bad rep.

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:12.401
We out here coming to bring
the Brussels to the hustle.

00:01:12.401 --> 00:01:13.978
Let's get these haters out here

00:01:13.978 --> 00:01:15.267
and turn them into lovers.

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:17.981
We hear you might have some vegetables

00:01:17.981 --> 00:01:19.737
that are not your favorite.

00:01:19.737 --> 00:01:21.905
- They've not had one
single Brussels sprout

00:01:21.905 --> 00:01:23.271
that I've ever enjoyed.

00:01:23.271 --> 00:01:24.291
- [Yadi] Not one?

00:01:24.291 --> 00:01:25.124
- [Kyle] No.

00:01:25.124 --> 00:01:26.861
- I think they smell terrible.

00:01:26.861 --> 00:01:28.128
- Ooh they smell like what?

00:01:28.128 --> 00:01:28.970
- Garbage.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:29.820
- It's like a little baby cabbage.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:30.653
It's like, "Hi!"
- Well I don't like

00:01:30.653 --> 00:01:31.894
I don't like cabbage so.

00:01:31.894 --> 00:01:32.727
- Like babies?

00:01:32.727 --> 00:01:34.688
- I don't like babies. (laughing)

00:01:34.688 --> 00:01:38.071
I am like beyond picky,
but it's all in my head.

00:01:38.071 --> 00:01:38.904
It's all about texture.

00:01:38.904 --> 00:01:39.737
- [Ross] Yes it is

00:01:39.737 --> 00:01:40.570
- And temperature.

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:41.636
- What are some of the ways

00:01:41.636 --> 00:01:43.821
you've eaten Brussels sprouts before?

00:01:43.821 --> 00:01:46.085
- I've eaten it like the really gross way

00:01:46.085 --> 00:01:48.743
where you just microwave them and then

00:01:48.743 --> 00:01:49.905
put it out there.

00:01:49.905 --> 00:01:51.487
- Wait, who, no.

00:01:51.487 --> 00:01:53.653
What are some flavors that you like?

00:01:53.653 --> 00:01:54.486
- [Ross] What makes you happy?

00:01:54.486 --> 00:01:55.849
- I like spicy food a lot.

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:56.740
- Ooh, okay.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.266
- I love crunchy things.

00:01:58.266 --> 00:02:00.762
- I'm like a savory over
sweet kind of person.

00:02:00.762 --> 00:02:01.595
- Savory over sweet.

00:02:01.595 --> 00:02:02.961
- Are you a strict vegetarian?

00:02:02.961 --> 00:02:03.996
- I eat seafood,

00:02:03.996 --> 00:02:05.125
but that's it.
- Oh, okay.

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:07.542
It's gonna be alright, ready?

00:02:08.519 --> 00:02:09.734
(loud exhaling)

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:11.673
May the odds be ever in our

00:02:11.673 --> 00:02:12.873
flavor.
- Flavor.

00:02:12.873 --> 00:02:14.305
(laughing)

00:02:14.305 --> 00:02:16.888
(upbeat music)

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.755
- I love to mix in
sofrito Caribbean flavors.

00:02:20.755 --> 00:02:22.434
Lots of spices and seasonings

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:24.799
that our contestants said that they loved.

00:02:24.799 --> 00:02:25.965
So I'm gonna mix that with something

00:02:25.965 --> 00:02:28.415
that they absolutely hate
which is Brussels sprouts

00:02:28.415 --> 00:02:31.009
and see if we can, not hide it,

00:02:31.009 --> 00:02:33.942
but celebrate and tuck
it at the same time.

00:02:33.942 --> 00:02:36.495
I'm making a shaved Brussels slaw

00:02:36.495 --> 00:02:38.419
with some red onions and then I'm making

00:02:38.419 --> 00:02:40.863
a Brussels sprout slider,

00:02:40.863 --> 00:02:43.476
and Old Bay Brussels chippies.

00:02:43.476 --> 00:02:44.934
A lot of what people don't like

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:46.800
is like the texture and the shape

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.722
so by using this mandolin here

00:02:48.722 --> 00:02:50.382
I've already deconstructed the shape

00:02:50.382 --> 00:02:52.820
and we're gonna make it rain sprouts.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:54.980
- I am making a Brussels sprout salad.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.144
So it's practically deep
fried Brussels sprouts

00:02:57.144 --> 00:03:00.043
with some cilantro, mint,
some chili-lime dressing

00:03:00.043 --> 00:03:01.428
like Southeast Asian style.

00:03:01.428 --> 00:03:03.402
Traditionally we use pork jowl

00:03:03.402 --> 00:03:04.885
which is right under here,

00:03:04.885 --> 00:03:07.480
but today I'm gonna be
using bacon and pancetta.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:08.992
So I'm just trying to
bring all these flavors

00:03:08.992 --> 00:03:11.185
so that people can understand
that Brussels sprouts

00:03:11.185 --> 00:03:12.341
are not that bad.

00:03:12.341 --> 00:03:14.013
And I understand that
we do have a vegetarian

00:03:14.013 --> 00:03:15.781
in our panel of judges, but you don't have

00:03:15.781 --> 00:03:18.118
to put in any meat in this salad

00:03:18.118 --> 00:03:19.339
which is actually really good.

00:03:19.339 --> 00:03:21.703
So you can stay healthy
and enjoy Brussels sprouts

00:03:21.703 --> 00:03:22.601
at the same time.

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:24.536
I'm deep frying the Brussels sprouts

00:03:24.536 --> 00:03:26.165
in just plain canola oil.

00:03:26.165 --> 00:03:27.539
That takes away some of the bitterness

00:03:27.539 --> 00:03:29.069
and when you hit it with the salt and acid

00:03:29.069 --> 00:03:31.000
and all the herbs it really brings out

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.917
the best flavor it could possibly be.

00:03:32.917 --> 00:03:34.537
- I brought my Caribbean flavors

00:03:34.537 --> 00:03:38.028
with my homemade adobo and
sofrito inside of my panko.

00:03:38.028 --> 00:03:40.403
Then I have my American
flavors with my slider

00:03:40.403 --> 00:03:41.842
and my Brussels sprout fries

00:03:41.842 --> 00:03:43.159
and now I'm bringing the Asian flavors

00:03:43.159 --> 00:03:44.647
with what I'm doing to the shrimp.

00:03:44.647 --> 00:03:46.085
I'm bringing some garlic, some honey,

00:03:46.085 --> 00:03:47.665
some soy sauce, some ginger.

00:03:47.665 --> 00:03:48.680
Pow pow pow.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:51.170
That was a technical cooking term.

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:53.753
(upbeat music)

00:03:56.394 --> 00:03:59.924
This is the American meets
Caribbean Brussels sprouts.

00:03:59.924 --> 00:04:02.004
Everyday we hustlin', Brusselin plate.

00:04:02.004 --> 00:04:03.551
You got your Brussels sprout slider,

00:04:03.551 --> 00:04:05.574
your Old Bay Brussels sprout chippies,

00:04:05.574 --> 00:04:08.391
a miso-maple butter sauce, a shaved slaw,

00:04:08.391 --> 00:04:10.825
and some jalapeno in your face.

00:04:10.825 --> 00:04:13.651
- I just pretty much made a
fried Brussels sprout salad.

00:04:13.651 --> 00:04:15.229
I kept it Southeast
Asian with the flavors,

00:04:15.229 --> 00:04:16.772
hit it with chili-lime dressing.

00:04:16.772 --> 00:04:18.250
For my non-vegetarian homies

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:20.713
I put some bacon and pancetta lardons.

00:04:20.713 --> 00:04:22.138
This is toasted rice powder.

00:04:22.138 --> 00:04:25.248
It adds a little bit more extra flair

00:04:25.248 --> 00:04:26.998
and we are done.

00:04:27.862 --> 00:04:31.445
(intense electronic music)

00:04:37.412 --> 00:04:38.632
- You don't even really taste

00:04:38.632 --> 00:04:40.654
the Brussels sprouts in the patty.

00:04:40.654 --> 00:04:41.736
- I said I like crunchy.

00:04:41.736 --> 00:04:43.831
She listened to me, she
made it extra crunchy.

00:04:43.831 --> 00:04:46.355
- I try to be the people's chef.

00:04:46.355 --> 00:04:49.938
(intense electronic music)

00:04:55.527 --> 00:04:56.360
- Mmm!

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:57.193
- It's sweet.

00:04:57.193 --> 00:04:58.701
- At a restaurant someone put this down

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:01.861
I'd be like, "Hell no.
I'm not touching this,"

00:05:01.861 --> 00:05:04.787
but it has really nice
flavor, really nice spice.

00:05:04.787 --> 00:05:07.611
It's like sweet and savory
kinda mixed together.

00:05:07.611 --> 00:05:08.968
- Exactly what I was going for.

00:05:08.968 --> 00:05:09.868
- I'm diggin' it.

00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:11.928
- First dish, so good, delicious.

00:05:11.928 --> 00:05:13.102
I loved the texture of it,

00:05:13.102 --> 00:05:14.681
especially the chippies on the side.

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:15.569
I thought it was great.

00:05:15.569 --> 00:05:17.371
The second dish, when you
put that down on the table

00:05:17.371 --> 00:05:19.275
I was like, "Hmm, cut!"

00:05:19.275 --> 00:05:21.059
The pressure was on,
the cameras were rolling

00:05:21.059 --> 00:05:23.067
so I took a bite and
I'm so glad that I did.

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:24.480
I just want blinders on 'cause I don't

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:25.675
wanna make anybody feel bad.

00:05:25.675 --> 00:05:27.022
- Aw, come on. (laughing)

00:05:27.022 --> 00:05:29.091
- The second dish is my favorite.

00:05:29.091 --> 00:05:30.837
- As a vegetarian I'm always open

00:05:30.837 --> 00:05:32.651
to different slider options

00:05:32.651 --> 00:05:35.999
and this was delicious
and the chips on the side

00:05:35.999 --> 00:05:38.369
were a really nice added bonus.

00:05:38.369 --> 00:05:40.852
The second dish I also loved as well.

00:05:40.852 --> 00:05:43.825
I'm a big fan of vegetables
and salads and everything.

00:05:43.825 --> 00:05:47.325
While both were incredible, the creativity

00:05:48.582 --> 00:05:51.588
of the first dish really
struck a chord with me.

00:05:51.588 --> 00:05:52.596
That's my favorite.

00:05:52.596 --> 00:05:54.160
- A slider is something I really like

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:56.243
and so to do like a
Brussels sprout take on it

00:05:56.243 --> 00:05:57.930
was like really cool for me

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:00.354
and then the salad really shocked me

00:06:00.354 --> 00:06:04.224
because I was like looking
at a full Brussels sprout

00:06:04.224 --> 00:06:07.784
and I was, you expect me
to put this in my mouth?

00:06:07.784 --> 00:06:09.973
But the flavors were amazing.

00:06:09.973 --> 00:06:12.348
They were the spices all mixed together

00:06:12.348 --> 00:06:14.124
and they were like savory and sweet,

00:06:14.124 --> 00:06:16.979
but I think I have to go with the salad.

00:06:16.979 --> 00:06:18.817
I was literally eating a Brussels sprout

00:06:18.817 --> 00:06:21.240
straight up and it was
amazing and I was shocked.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:23.133
I'm glad we got to
change your guys' minds.

00:06:23.133 --> 00:06:24.231
- [All] Yeah!

00:06:24.231 --> 00:06:27.326
- Can we get some Brussels
spirit fingers going here?

00:06:27.326 --> 00:06:28.385
(laughing)

00:06:28.385 --> 00:06:29.475
Everyday we Brusselin'.

00:06:29.475 --> 00:06:30.308
- Yeah.

00:06:30.308 --> 00:06:33.305
- So Chef Ross, did we
hustle for these Brussels?

00:06:33.305 --> 00:06:35.388
- It's all in the muscle.

00:06:36.673 --> 00:06:39.590
(electronic music)

